摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"A pre-execution guard for AI coding agents. It blocks destructive Git and file system commands, plus common attempts to access sensitive files, before a tool call runs. Supports Amp Code, Antigravity CLI, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, DeepSeek Harness, Devin CLI, GitHub Copilot CLI","id":"gh:1122873619","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"cc-safety-net","slug":"kenryu42/cc-safety-net","topics":["ai-agents","ai-safety","antigravity","claude","claude-code","claude-code-plugin","codex","codex-cli","coding-agent","cursor","developer-tools","dsh","dsh-plugin","guardrails","hermes-agent","hooks","openclaw","opencode","pi-extension","security"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"A pre-execution guard for AI coding agents. It blocks destructive Git and file system commands, plus"},{"id":"p1s2","text":" common attempts to access sensitive files, before a tool call runs. Supports Amp Code, Antigravity "},{"id":"p1s3","text":"CLI, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, DeepSeek Harness, Devin CLI, GitHub Copilot CLI"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"**English** · 简体中文 · 日本語"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/353c1441-9156-483c-b8e5-32fce7905a83"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"CC Safety Net (Coding CLI Safety Net) blocks destructive commands and access to secrets such as SSH "},{"id":"p4s2","text":"keys and `.env` files before the tool call runs. It parses what the command does. Wrapping the comma"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"nd or reordering flags does not hide it. A broken config file falls back to safe defaults instead of"},{"id":"p4s4","text":" stopping your agent. It is not a sandbox: it does not contain processes, set filesystem permissions"},{"id":"p4s5","text":", or watch network egress."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> **Full documentation →** covers installation, configuration, reference material, guides,"},{"id":"p5s2","text":" and the security model. This README is the short version."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Supported coding CLIs"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"CC Safety Net supports these coding agent CLIs on Windows, macOS, and Linux."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"Amp Code"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"Antigravity CLI"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Claude Code"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Codex"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Cursor"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Devin CLI"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Factory Droid"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"Gemini CLI"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"GitHub Copilot CLI"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Grok Build"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Hermes Agent"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Kimi Code"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"OpenClaw"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"OpenCode"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Pi"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"- **Blocks destructive commands** such as `git reset --hard`, `git push --force`, and `rm -rf` on da"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"ngerous targets, and install scripts piped from the internet (`curl … | bash`), even inside `bash -c"},{"id":"p26s3","text":"` or `python -c`. See Blocked commands.\n- **Blocks secret access** to SSH keys, `.env` files, `~/.aw"},{"id":"p26s4","text":"s`, and coding-CLI credentials, from the shell and from the agent's file tools. See Secret protectio"},{"id":"p26s5","text":"n.\n- **Tunes the policy in a GUI.** Run `npx cc-safety-net gui` to pick the Standard, Strict, or Par"},{"id":"p26s6","text":"anoid preset and turn rules on or off. See Dashboard.\n- **Adds blocks through rulebooks**: official "},{"id":"p26s7","text":"packs for Terraform, AWS, gcloud, and Azure, or your own JSON. See Official rulebooks.\n- **Shares po"},{"id":"p26s8","text":"licy through git.** Commit `.cc-safety-net/` so clones and cloud sessions get the same rules. See Te"},{"id":"p26s9","text":"am setup.\n- **Embeds in your own tools.** Call `checkCommand` from Node.js without installing the ho"},{"id":"p26s10","text":"ok. See Library API."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"You need Node.js 22 or higher. Install into the coding CLIs on this machine, then check that protect"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"s 22 or higher. Install into the coding CLIs on this machine, then check that protection is working:"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"Update with `npx -y cc-safety-net@latest update` and uninstall with `npx -y cc-safety-net uninstall`"},{"id":"p30s2","text":". Keep the `@latest` qualifier: a bare `cc-safety-net` spec can run an older copy from the npx cache"},{"id":"p30s3","text":". Per-CLI requirements are in Installation."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"## Development"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"See CONTRIBUTING.md to report a bug or request a feature."},{"id":"p33s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"MIT"}],"truncated":false}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
